    "activation_raw": null,
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "Gu Masters use the whale enslavement Gu to control flying blue whales and put them to work in a caravan.",
        "chapters": [
          260
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "fac_gu_masters"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Flying blue whales live above the nine heavens of the eastern seas and have a peaceful and mild temperament. A whale is huge, like a small mountain, and the entire caravan hides inside its body as it travels in the sky. That route is less dangerous and faster than a caravan moving through the forests. A flying blue whale consumes up to five hundred kilograms of food a day, so only a large-sized clan can afford to feed them.",
        "chapters": [
          260
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "effect",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
      },
      {
        "text": "In the entire southern border, only Yi clan owned flying blue whales. Yi clan is one of the overlords of the southern border, almost the same status as Shang clan, and had a close relationship with the forces in the eastern seas.",
        "chapters": [
          260
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
